          "kicker": "Fitness boost",
          "heading": "Tommy Freeman in frame for rematch after missing England's 37-12 win",
          "body": "The Northampton wing started nine Tests in a row this year before being rotated out against Japan, then a thigh issue forced him out in the hours before kick-off last Saturday, with Harlequins' Cadan Murley impressing in his place. Freeman is in Steve Borthwick's 37-strong squad for this weekend's play-off with New Zealand, as is Fin Smith, who went off after 55 minutes with cramp. Of the 64 fans in the app who answered after full time, 97% were buzzing."
