      "edition": "Wednesday 25 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Final build-up",
          "heading": "Thomas Ramos back at Marcoussis as Moefana rejects France favourites tag",
          "body": "Yoram Moefana says South Africa remain the world's top side ahead of this weekend's Nations Championship final at Twickenham. He expects the intensity to climb as the Springboks chase revenge for their defeat at Saint-Denis a fortnight ago, and warns that the threat is their whole collective rather than any one player. The Bordeaux centre insists the squad has stayed humble, with the week's focus on France's own game and the small details still to sharpen. Ramos returned to Marcoussis this week."
